  "rationale": "`assets/skills/habeas-bootstrap-requirements/SKILL.md` is a bundled skill. It has front matter, so it is a site of `requirements.cli.skill_conventions.workflow`, and the requirement applies.\n\nThe file has one H1, `# Bootstrap requirements`. Under it, the first H2 section is `## Workflow`, which is `section[Bootstrap%20requirements]/section[Workflow]`. The other H2 sections (Inventories, Proposing requirements, Tagging, Report, Gotchas) all come after it. Before `## Workflow` there is only a short orienting paragraph and a pointer to the habeas skill's testing guidance. Both sit under the H1 title and are not sections, so no other section precedes the workflow.\n\nThe workflow is ordered steps: a numbered checklist, items 1 to 9. It has a lead-in that says which steps run once and which repeat per area. Step 7 has nested lettered sub-steps (a to c).\n\nThe violation-query leads do not apply here, because nothing breaks the requirement. I found no gap.",
